// @METADATA:name        = paper_p6
// @METADATA:description = Program P6 from Figure 8 of the paper.
//                         Illustrates observe-nontermination dependence
//                         with a nonterminating loop inside a conditional
//                         and an observe after the conditional.
//                         When x>=4: while(y=4) may not terminate.
//                         When x<4:  skip.
//                         After the conditional: observe(y>2) conditions
//                         on y. Under ns, the while predicate is an
//                         obsntd_nt source and generates obsntd edges.
//                         The if-predicate (x>=4) is scd-dependent on
//                         observe(y>2) since nonterminating path never
//                         reaches the observe. Under nids, wcd may not
//                         add this dependency. Under ni, only the observe
//                         is a source.
// @METADATA:reference   = Masud and Olmedo (2026) Static Nontermination-
//                         (In)Sensitive Slicing of Probabilistic Programs.
//                         Figure 8, Program P6.
// @METADATA:criterion   = x
// @METADATA:expected    = ns: x kept via return; if-predicate kept via
//                         scd on observe (nonterminating path never
//                         reaches observe); while kept via obsntd_nt;
//                         y kept via observe(y>2) and while guard;
//                         nids: observe(y>2) kept; if-predicate may be
//                         sliced (wcd does not add scd-only deps);
//                         while may be sliced; y kept via observe;
//                         ni: observe(y>2) kept as source; nonterminating
//                         while NOT a source; most aggressive slice
// @METADATA:tags        = observe, nontermination, conditional, obsntd,
//                         paper-example, figure-8, ns-vs-nids-vs-ni,
//                         key-example

x :~ unif[1, 4];
y :~ unif[1, 4];
if x >= 4 then
    while y = 4 do
        skip;
    end
else
    skip;
end
observe(y > 2);
return x;